// NPC -> GLB model mapping.
//
// createNPCMesh falls back to `mapping[npcKey] || npcKey`, so a cast key with
// no entry here looks for a GLB literally named e.g. "NPC_KLAUS", finds
// nothing, and returns an EMPTY GROUP. The character is then invisible with no
// error. Six speaking characters were in that state, including NPC_KLAUS, who
// is cast in shift_1_teach / shift_2_anticipate / shift_3_test, the three
// warehouse scenes and the exact scene ?quickstart=1 drops a judge into.
//
// character-male-c is deliberately left unassigned: it is a blue police
// uniform with a cap and badge, which read as law enforcement on Nico, a
// student. Do not map a civilian character to it.
//
// build/verify.js asserts every cast key in story.json resolves to a real GLB.
